 "title": "How to get information out of anyone",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator analyzes a scene from James Bond to explain how to get information out of anyone by starting with a mistake. By admitting a harmless error upfront, you lower the other person's defensiveness and turn them into helper mode, leading them to share information willingly.",
 "key_points": [
  "Start with a mistake, such as saying 'I bumped into a car'.",
  "Admitting a mistake upfront lowers the other person's defensiveness.",
  "It changes your image from a potential threat to someone human and harmless.",
  "Addressing the mistake as a problem you have switches the other person's brain from defense mode to help mode.",
  "Make a confession and frame the information you want as the solution to the problem your confession exposes."
 ],
 "content": "Welcome to the Ocean Club, sir. Checking in? Yes, but it's a spur of the moment thing and I haven't got a reservation. Okay. We have an ocean view villa. Perfect. Could you do me a favor? I was here for dinner last night and I parked my car next to a very beautiful 1964 Aston Martin and I'm ashamed to say I nicked the door. You wouldn't happen to know- Mr. Demetrius? Right. If he hasn't noticed, I'm not sure I'd mention it. He's not the type to take bad news well. But if I felt compelled to find him, he has a house just up at the beach. Notice how James Bond gets this receptionist to spill where a guy lives. He doesn't directly ask where is he. He essentially says, look, I made a mistake, I bumped into a car. And here's why this works so well. When you admit a mistake up front, the other person's brain instantly switches off its guard. You go from looking like a potential threat to looking totally human and harmless. And not only that, but when you address the mistake as a problem you have, you make the other person's brain go from defense mode to help mode. So the receptionist gives not only the guy's name, but also his address completely on her own. If you want to use this yourself and get someone to open up and trust you fast, try this. Make a confession and frame the information you want as the solution to the problem your confession exposes. Use this responsibly. Follow if you want to become a more effective communicator. Text shown on screen: How to get information out of anyone, watch what she reveals, start with the mistake, I bumped into a car, less defensive, from defense to help, watch her answer, I made a mistake, Make people comfortable sharing secrets with you, Follow to become an effective communicator, Make a note of this post.",
